# Xcode
#
# gitignore contributors: remember to update Global/Xcode.gitignore, Objective-C.gitignore & Swift.gitignore

## User settings
xcuserdata/

## Obj-C/Swift specific
*.hmap

## App packaging
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM

# CocoaPods
#
# We recommend against adding the Pods directory to your .gitignore. However
# you should judge for yourself, the pros and cons are mentioned at:
# https://guides.cocoapods.org/using/using-cocoapods.html#should-i-check-the-pods-directory-into-source-control
#
# Pods/
#
# Add this line if you want to avoid checking in source code from the Xcode workspace
# *.xcworkspace

# Carthage
#
# Add this line if you want to avoid checking in source code from Carthage dependencies.
# Carthage/Checkouts

Carthage/Build/

# fastlane
#
# It is recommended to not store the screenshots in the git repo.
# Instead, use fastlane to re-generate the screenshots whenever they are needed.
# For more information about the recommended setup visit:
# https://docs.fastlane.tools/best-practices/source-control/#source-control

fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots/**/*.png
fastlane/test_output

# Xcode build products (CI uses -derivedDataPath build/DerivedData)
build/

# Custom derivedDataPath dirs created during local sandbox-bypass builds.
# Mirrors the pattern `xcodebuild -derivedDataPath "$PWD/<name>" build` uses
# in the harness scripts. Covers macOS and iOS sim builds, with headroom for
# future variants. (iOS demos were migrated out on 2026-09-08; the
# `build-ios-*` patterns are kept as a no-op safety net in case they return.)
build-*/
build-*-dd/

# Specs — internal SDD docs only. None of this is shipped to customers.
# The repo's `.md` files in `specs/` (S0/S1/S1b/S2 plus `README.md`) are
# written in Chinese as the internal AI-assistant collaboration protocol
# (Spec-Driven Development). Customers should never see them. The whole
# directory is ignored; rebuild from the conversation on a new machine.
#
# Sub-paths covered:
#   - specs/*.spec.md, specs/README.md   (SDD markdown, all Chinese)
#   - specs/evidence/**/*.png            (13+ MB per spec; regenerable)
#   - specs/.DS_Store, **/.DS_Store      (macOS Finder cruft)
specs/

# WorkBuddy session memory. Files in here (`.workbuddy/memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md`
# daily logs + `MEMORY.md`) are WorkBuddy-managed state, not project source.
# 184 KB total today, but the contents are local to this machine's
# WorkBuddy session — regenerate from the conversation when needed.
.workbuddy/

## AI assistant state (per-machine, never in git)
# Mirrors the enumeration in `STYLE.md` → Rule 0 → "AI assistant state files".
# Any state produced by an AI coding tool is local-only; do not commit it.
# When a new tool is adopted, add its state path here in the same PR that
# documents it in STYLE.md.
#
# WorkBuddy (per-project) — already covered above as `.workbuddy/`.
# WorkBuddy (global bootstrap lives outside the repo, but `AGENTS.md`-
# style files at the repo root are still local-only).
#
# Note: `AGENTS.md` is the local AI assistant entry point. It is intentionally
# gitignored (per-client / per-machine customization). The canonical template
# lives in `STYLE.md` Rule 0 → "AI assistant onboarding" → "`AGENTS.md`
# template". On a new machine, recreate it from that template.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
